This is NOT a Dockerfile or docker-compose.yml issue. The error occurs during repository setup BEFORE the Docker build starts. The deployment agent needs to clean up the stale git lock file. Add this to your deployment_agent.py in the _setup_repository method before git clone:

import shutil
from pathlib import Path

# Clean up stale git lock files
repo_dir = Path(f'/tmp/recursai-deployments/{app_name}')
if repo_dir.exists():
    lock_file = repo_dir / '.git' / 'shallow.lock'
    if lock_file.exists():
        lock_file.unlink()
    # Or safer: remove entire directory and start fresh
    shutil.rmtree(repo_dir)

Then proceed with git clone.